2. Test Strategy & Phases
Phase 1: Smoke & Sanity Testing (Build Verification)
* Objective: Ensure the repository builds cleanly and core routes/components load without crashing.
* Test Cases:
   * TC-SMK-01: Repository build verification (npm install / gradle build / package manager check depending on stack).
   * TC-SMK-02: Application startup and initialization of core layout/design tokens.
   * TC-SMK-03: Basic navigation check (ensuring no dead-end routes or broken dependency injections).
Phase 2: Functional System Testing
* Objective: Verify that all integrated features perform as expected based on system specifications.
* Test Categories:
   * UI/UX & Design System Compliance: Verify that typography, spacing, color variables, and components match the yds-design tokens accurately.
   * State Management & Data Flow: Test component state retention across screens, navigation transitions, and asynchronous fetching/local storage sync.
   * User Interaction Flows: Validate buttons, inputs, gesture physics (if mobile/touch-driven), and modal behaviors.
Phase 3: Non-Functional Testing
* Performance & Load Testing:
   * Measure initial bundle size/startup latency.
   * Monitor memory leaks during prolonged navigation or continuous media/data rendering.
* Compatibility Testing:
   * Cross-browser evaluation (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) or multi-resolution viewport testing for responsive web/mobile views.
* Accessibility (a11y) Testing:
   * Check color contrast ratios against design system specifications.
   * Validate screen-reader labels, semantic HTML elements, and keyboard navigation support.
